    "text": "In the WorldLines paper, the phrase 'translating long-term memory into embodied plans' is not listed among the fundamental research challenges or as a standalone problem statement.",
    "topic": "Problem framing"
  },
  {
    "text": "The paper exclusively introduces the translation as a technical step within the proposed solution to mitigate partial observability and overwritten world states.",
    "topic": "Method vs. challenge"
  },
  {
    "text": "No section of the paper frames the translation difficulty as an 'instrumental challenge' or any category of challenge; that terminology is an external interpretation.",
    "topic": "Terminology"
  },
  {
    "text": "The paper's abstract and introduction state that the core problems are partial observability and catastrophic forgetting in world models, with the translation serving as a mechanism to address them.",
    "topic": "Core vs. derived"
  }
]
